sddm-theme-lingmo (1.5.0.lingmo.3) helium; urgency=medium

  * Actually enable the theme on install: ship
    /etc/sddm.conf.d/10-lingmo-theme.conf (a dpkg conffile) containing
    [General] InputMethod=qtvirtualkeyboard and GreeterEnvironment with
    QML2_IMPORT_PATH=/usr/share/sddm/themes/lingmo/components/ plus
    QT_IM_MODULE=qtvirtualkeyboard, and [Theme] Current=lingmo.
    Without the [General] pair the greeter cannot resolve the theme's components/
    directory (it overrides the virtual keyboard style) and SDDM silently falls
    back to its default theme, so installing the package appeared to do nothing.
    A snippet under /etc/sddm.conf.d/ is used instead of /etc/sddm.conf because
    other SDDM themes write that file too.

 -- Lingmo OS Team <team@lingmo.org>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:11:16 +0800

sddm-theme-lingmo (1.5.0.lingmo.2) helium; urgency=medium

  * Do not require lrelease at build time. The OBS build failed with
    "lrelease6: not found" (exit 127) because that binary is not in the
    build environment, even though qt6-l10n-tools is a build dependency.
    debian/rules now compiles the catalogues when lrelease6, lrelease or
    /usr/lib/qt6/bin/lrelease is available and otherwise keeps the
    translations/*.qm that are committed in the source tree, so the
    package always ships usable translations.

 -- Lingmo OS Team <team@lingmo.org>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:27:53 +0800

sddm-theme-lingmo (1.5.0.lingmo.1) helium; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging for Lingmo OS, based on SilentSDDM 1.5.0
    (https://github.com/uiriansan/SilentSDDM).
  * Rebrand to Lingmo: the theme name, Theme-Id and install directory
    are now "lingmo". Because lingmo-sddm-theme already provides
    /usr/share/sddm/themes/lingmo, this package declares
    Conflicts/Replaces against it.
  * Chinese translations (zh_CN, zh_TW, zh_HK). The theme's own strings
    are wrapped in qsTr() and translations/*.ts are compiled to *.qm at
    build time, so the login screen follows the system locale.
  * Normalise line endings to LF. Upstream files arrived with CRLF,
    which broke install.sh and test.sh with "bad interpreter".
  * Ship the bundled Red Hat Display fonts under
    /usr/share/fonts/truetype.

 -- Lingmo OS Team <team@lingmo.org>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:19:07 +0800
